עלה אלדי נפתלי בן ראי עלי בתים\nL2341@P107: II.L.1.9.4.\nL2342@P107:  ̇ה̇י ̇ו ̇א חרוף ̇ת ̇פ ̇כ ̇ד ̇ג ̇לב כמא מכצוצה חרוף לה ענדהם פאלריש\nL2343@P107-108: קבל תעמל מנהא חרפאן חרוף ̇אלח פהדה ̇ן ̇ל ̇ס ̇ט ̇ת ̇צ ̇ז ̇ד והי 54596 Hidāyat al-Qāriʾ (Long Version)\nL2344@P108: and ̇ן ̇ל. Two of these eight letters operate both before the resh\nL2345@P108: and after it, namely ̇ן ̇ל, and the six other letters before the resh.\nL2346@P108: The eight letters aˤect the resh only when shewa is under it or\nL2347@P108: (when shewa is) under the eight letters that are speci˚c to it.\nL2348@P108: II.L.1.9.5.\nL2349@P108: The light resh in their tradition is (in words) such as ה֛ ָב ָכּ ְר ֶמּ ַה ם ֹ֧ת ְר\nL2350@P108: ‘Harness the chariot!’ (Micah 1.13), ה ָלְי ֽ ָל י ֵיס ִ֥ס ְר’ drops of the night’\nL2351@P108: (Cant. 5.2), ֙ה ֶנ ְשׁ ִמּ ַה ת ֶב֤ ֶכּ ְר ִמ ְבּ’ in his second chariot’ (Gen. 41.43).\nL2352@P108: Such cases and similar ones are their normal pronunciation of\nL2353@P108: the letter, for they consider it to be the light resh.\nL2354@P108: II.L.1.9.6.\nL2355@P108: The major resh in their tradition are cases such as ֙ם ֶית ִא ְרּ ַה’ Have\nL2356@P108: you seen?’ (2 Kings 6.32), הּ ֑ ָמ ִע ְרּ ַה’ to irritate her’ (1 Sam. 1.6),\nL2357@P108: and the like.\nL2358@P108: II.L.1.9.7.\nL2359@P108: The grade between two grades (of the resh) where dalet precedes\nL2360@P108: it are cases such as וֹן֜יּ ִצ י ֵ֙כ ְר ַדּ’ the roads to Zion’ (Lam. 1.4), וֹ ֖כּ ְר ַדּ\nL2361@P108: ‘his way’ (Gen. 24.21), וֹן ֥א ְר ִד ְל’ to contempt’ (Dan. 12.2). Cases\nL2362@P108: with zayin are יףִ֥ז ְרַז’ dripping’ (Psa. 72.6), T ֶל ֹ֖מּ ַל וֹ ֛ע ְר ַזּ ִמ’ any of his\nL2363@P108: oˤspring to Molech’ (Lev. 20.2), ק ֹ֑רְזִי’ He scatters’ (Isa. 28.25).\nL2364@P108: Cases with ṣade are ף ֣ ֵר ְצ ַמ’ the crucible’ (Prov. 17.3), ף ֹ֣ר ְצ ִכּ’ as\nL2365@P108: testing’ (Zech. 13.9), ת ַ֔פ ְר֣ ָד־צ ַע’ as far as Zarephath’ (Obd. 1.20).\nL2366@P108: Cases of tav are ַµי ֣ ִק  ְר ַתּ’ you spread out’ (Job 37.18